{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109834","id":2763700717,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6kurnt","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109834","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109834.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109834.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109834","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109834/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109834/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109834/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/a4e8a7cd6e81a0ade38dbf95cae9cdb75217a96b","number":109834,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add workflow support for OpenHarmony export templates","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch in priority.\r\n\r\nRelevant fixes are cherry-picked for stable branches as needed by maintainers.\r\n\r\nTo speed up the contribution process and avoid CI errors, please set up pre-commit hooks locally:\r\nhttps://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/contributing/development/code_style_guidelines.html\r\n-->\r\n\r\nFollow-up to #108553.\r\n\r\nProvides a workflow for building OpenHarmony export templates, making it easier for users to test without having to compile editors and export templates.\r\n\r\n## Export the project\r\n\r\n### Preparation\r\n\r\n1. Download the editor and export templates from the [artifacts](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109834/checks/) in Actions.[^1]\r\n2. Download Commandline Tools, which currently requires API level 17+, that is, version 5.0.5+.[^2]\r\n    - https://repo.huaweicloud.com/openharmony/ohpm/ (No registration required)\r\n    - https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/download/command-line-tools-for-hmos (Registration required)\r\n3. After extracting all the files, you will get a directory called `command-line-tools`, whose path is the path you need to fill in `export/openharmony/openharmony_tool_path` in the editor settings.\r\n4. Download JDK, only JDK 17 is supported.[^3]\r\n5. Please fill in the JDK path in `export/openharmony/java_sdk_path` in the editor settings.\r\n6. Enable `textures/vram_compression/import_etc2_astc` in the project settings;\r\n\r\n### Export the unsigned hap/app\r\n\r\nAdds an OpenHarmony preset in the [export menu](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/export/exporting_projects.html#export-menu). \r\n\r\nCheck **Advanced Options**, and then specify `custom_template/debug` and `custom_template/release` as the export templates you just downloaded.[^4]\r\n\r\nMake sure the export path does not contain special characters such as spaces.\r\n\r\n### Prepare the material files required for signature[^5]\r\n\r\nSignature material files can be generated by [DevEco Studio](https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/download/deveco-studio), but unfortunately DevEco Studio is not available on Linux.\r\n\r\nYou can also generate these files manually by following the steps below.\r\n\r\n1. Create a keystore (.p12) file; [^6]\r\n    ```shell\r\n    keytool -genkeypair -alias \"key_alias\" -keyalg EC -sigalg \"SHA256withECDSA\" -keystore \"store_file.p12\" -storetype pkcs12 -storepass \"StorePassword\" -dname \"CN=myapp.example.com, OU=IT Department, O=My Company, L=City, ST=State, C=Country\" -keypass \"StorePassword\" -validity \"3650\"\r\n    ```\r\n2. Generate a certificate request (.csr) file;[^6][^7]\r\n    ```shell\r\n    keytool -certreq -alias \"key_alias\" -keystore \"store_file.p12\" -storetype pkcs12 -file \"test.csr\" -storepass \"StorePassword\"\r\n    ```\r\n3. Use the \"store_file.p12\" file and \"test.csr\" file generated in the previous two steps to apply for the certificate (.cer) and profile (.p7b) files in [AppGallery Connect](https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/cn/service/josp/agc/index.html). (Registration required)\r\n\r\n### Export the signed hap/app\r\n\r\nEnable `build/sign`. For the meaning and filling requirements of the fields, refer to [Manually Configuring the Signature Information](https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-signing#section112371245115818).\r\n\r\nTo manually sign the unsigned HAP file exported previously, refer to [Signing a HAP](https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-command-line-building-app#section103321051433).\r\n\r\n### Notice\r\n\r\nThe English version of the Harmony/OpenHarmony documentation may be outdated. Please refer to the Chinese version.\r\n\r\nIf you don't have a suitable test device, you can try the [cloud debugging service](https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/en/agconnect/) provided by AppGallery Connect. See [云调试](https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/cn/doc/app/agc-help-clouddebug-0000002235870046). But it requires you to upload signed release builds.[^8]\r\n\r\n[^1]: Usually you need to remove a layer of compression. The debug and release templates are named `openharmony_debug_arm64-v8a.zip` and `openharmony_release_arm64-v8a.zip` respectively.\r\n[^2]: It is recommended to download a higher version, which will give you more options when exporting.\r\n[^3]: Reference Chinese documentation, [配置JDK](https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/cn/doc/harmonyos-guides/ide-command-line-building-app#section195447475220). \r\n[^4]: You can also create directories in the [data](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/classes/class_editorpaths.html#class-editorpaths-method-get-data-dir) directory according to the path `export_templates/4.5.beta/` and move the export templates into the directory `4.5.beta`.\r\n[^5]: Can be skipped if `build/sign` is not enabled in the export preset.\r\n[^6]: Replace the string enclosed in double quotes on the command line as needed.\r\n[^7]: Ensure the values ​​of the same parameters in the two commands are the same.\r\n[^8]: Requirements see [前提条件](https://developer.huawei.com/consumer/cn/doc/app/agc-help-clouddebug-debugapp-0000002289629821#section112564349471).","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098009,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgwMDk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:buildsystem","name":"topic:buildsystem","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098255,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:platforms","name":"topic:platforms","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"h